# Example environment for local development
#
# === TrendForge app: Real X data via the secure proxy ===
# The /api/x-search endpoint (used by "SYNC REAL X", "TEST", and "LIVE REAL") needs X_BEARER_TOKEN.
#
# Best local dev:
#   source ~/.x-mcp.env
#   X_BEARER_TOKEN=PASTE_BEARER_HERE npx vercel dev
#
# Get a Bearer Token:
#   Option A (recommended for Vercel Production): https://developer.x.com → Your Project/App
#     → Keys and tokens → "Bearer Token" (App-only). Static, long-lived; valid until you
#     regenerate it in the portal. This is what X_BEARER_TOKEN expects.
#   Option B (local dev via xurl): stores the same long-lived app-only bearer locally:
#     source ~/.x-mcp.env
#     npx -y @xdevplatform/xurl auth app-only
#
# ⚠️  Do NOT use an OAuth 2.0 *user* token for X_BEARER_TOKEN (e.g. the output of
#     `npx -y @xdevplatform/xurl --app xapi token`). Those are short-lived and auto-refreshed
#     by the MCP bridge — pasting one into Vercel makes Sync all work briefly, then fail with
#     "unauthorized" until you replace it. Use the App-only Bearer Token instead.
#
# Then run the proxy + UI together:
#   X_BEARER_TOKEN=... npx vercel dev
#   Click "TEST" or "SYNC REAL X" in the app.
#
# === xapi MCP (for "ASK GROK + X MCP" + rich tools inside Grok) ===
# Credentials live in ~/.x-mcp.env (already has your X_CLIENT_ID / X_CLIENT_SECRET).
#
# One-time setup (run this in terminal):
#   source ~/.x-mcp.env
#   npx -y @xdevplatform/xurl auth oauth2 --app xapi
#
# IMPORTANT: In https://developer.x.com app settings (User authentication):
#   Enable OAuth 2.0
#   Add BOTH redirect URIs:
#     http://localhost:8080/callback
#     https://trendforge-opal.vercel.app/callback
#
# After browser consent succeeds, check:
#   source ~/.x-mcp.env && npx -y @xdevplatform/xurl auth status --app xapi
#
# Then restart this Grok session (or use /mcps modal + 'r' to refresh) so xapi MCP connects with 20+ tools.
#
# X_BEARER_TOKEN=   # direct override when using `npx vercel dev`
#
# === Spend cap (server-enforced; required for production real X) ===
# Hard monthly cap for X API spend (default 20 USD if unset).
# Requires Vercel KV (or Upstash Redis) bound to the project.
#
#   Vercel: Install "KV (Upstash Redis)" → Project Integrations
#   Then set the following env vars for Production + Preview:
#     KV_REST_API_URL=
#     KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
#   Optional:
#     X_SPEND_CAP_USD=20
#     # X_POST_COST_USD=0.005   # override per-post USD estimate if X changes pricing
#
# === Proxy abuse gates (no login; same-origin + rate limits by default) ===
# Both /api/x-search and /api/forge-chat accept same-origin requests only
# (browser Origin/Referer must match the deployment host).
# Optional hardening (names only — never commit values):
#   APP_ACCESS_TOKEN=      # when set, clients must send it as x-app-token
#   APP_ORIGIN=            # comma-separated allowed hosts/URLs (default: request host)
#   FORGE_ALLOWED_MODELS=  # e.g. grok-4.5,grok-4,grok-3 (server-side allowlist)
#   FORGE_MAX_TOKENS=      # per-request max_tokens cap (default 1000, ceiling 2000)
#   X_SEARCH_PER_HOUR=     # per-IP hourly cap for /api/x-search (default 60)
#   FORGE_CHAT_PER_HOUR=   # per-IP hourly cap for /api/forge-chat (default 30)
#   X_SEARCH_SESS_PER_HOUR=    # per-session caps for signed-in callers (defaults 300 / 120)
#   FORGE_CHAT_SESS_PER_HOUR=
#   SYNC_SESS_PER_HOUR=        # bookmark syncs per session per hour (default 10)
#   DIGEST_SESS_PER_HOUR=      # digest generations per session per hour (default 30)
#   THEMES_SESS_PER_HOUR=      # theme discoveries per session per hour (default 20)
#   BOOKMARKS_ASK_SESS_PER_HOUR=  # Grok-assisted searches per session per hour (default 30)
#   APP_BASE_URL=          # optional canonical base URL for the OAuth callback (default: request headers)
#   X_ALLOWED_USER_IDS=    # RESERVED, not enforced yet: optional comma-separated X user ids allowed to sign in
#
# === Bookmark Forge (Sign in with X via OAuth 2.0 + PKCE) ===
# Tokens stay server-side (encrypted in KV, httpOnly session cookie).
# Names only — never commit values:
#   X_CLIENT_ID=
#   X_CLIENT_SECRET=
#   SESSION_SECRET=        # 16+ chars; seals sessions server-side
#   CRON_SECRET=           # Bearer secret for /api/cron/weekly-digest
#   X_BOOKMARK_COST_USD=   # optional per-post bookmark cost override
#   X_USER_OWNS_APP=       # set "false" when the X app belongs to someone else ($0.005/post)
#
# === Grok forge (Content forge → LLM → Grok preset) ===
# Server-side proxy: POST /api/forge-chat → https://api.x.ai/v1/chat/completions
# Key never ships in the client bundle.
#
#   XAI_API_KEY=xai-... npx vercel dev
#   Vercel: vercel env add XAI_API_KEY
#
# Get a key: https://console.x.ai
# Default model: grok-4.5 (override in the forge panel).
# Optional: paste a session key in the UI (sessionStorage only) if env is unset.
#
# XAI_API_KEY=
